  "title": "Kourovka problem 12.72 (main)",
  "statement": {
    "representation": "pdf-text-entry",
    "text": "Let F be a soluble local hereditary formation of finite groups. Prove that F is\nradical if every finite soluble minimal non-F-group G is a minimal non-Nl(G)−1 -group.\nHere N is the formation of all finite nilpotent groups, and l(G) is the nilpotent length\nof G.                                                                  V. N. Semenchuk",
